---
// Three action kinds exist and no more: sound, webhook, run a command. There is no
// notification action and no native Shortcuts action — Shortcuts are reached through the
// webhook or the command. See crates/yamete-proto/src/config.rs.
---

<section id="actions">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Actions</p>
    <h2>Then something happens</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Three kinds of response, each filtered by how hard the hit was. Every one of them can
      read the slap it is responding to.
    </p>

    <div class="recipes">
      <article class="recipe card">
        <h3>Play a sound</h3>
        <p>
          Point it at files or a whole folder and it picks one each time, in order or at
          random, never the same one twice running. Volume can follow how hard you hit it.
        </p>
        <pre><code><span class="c"># out of the box</span>
/System/Library/
  Sounds/<span class="v">Sosumi.aiff</span></code></pre>
      </article>

      <article class="recipe card">
        <h3>Call a webhook</h3>
        <p>
          Any method, any headers, any body. The URL and the body are templated, so it can
          talk to Home Assistant, a Shortcut or an IFTTT hook without special-casing.
        </p>
        <pre><code><span class="c"># POST body</span>
&#123;
  "tier": "<span class="v">&#123;&#123;tier&#125;&#125;</span>",
  "g": <span class="v">&#123;&#123;peak_g&#125;&#125;</span>
&#125;</code></pre>
      </article>

      <article class="recipe card">
        <h3>Run a command</h3>
        <p>
          The slap arrives twice over: as environment variables for shell one-liners, and
          as a JSON object on stdin for anything that would rather parse it.
        </p>
        <pre><code><span class="c">$</span> osascript -e "set volume 0"
<span class="c">#</span> <span class="v">$YAMETE_TIER</span> → major
<span class="c">#</span> <span class="v">$YAMETE_PEAK_G</span> → 0.52</code></pre>
        <p class="mono meta">Behind an advanced switch</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="pair">
      <div class="detail card card--quiet">
        <h3>It waits 200 ms first</h3>
        <p>
          Detection is fast enough that a sound starts while the physical slap is still
          audible, and gets partly masked by it. The response wants to land after the
          impact, not on top of it. 200 ms was chosen by ear, and it is adjustable per
          action.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="detail card card--quiet">
        <h3>Severity and confidence are different questions</h3>
        <p>
          How many detectors agreed answers "was that an impact at all". How hard you hit
          it is amplitude, and that alone decides whether an action tagged
          <em>major</em> fires. Gating one on the other reported a real whack as a graze.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .recipes {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 270px), 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  .recipe {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.6rem;
  }

  .recipe h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .recipe p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  /* Pushes each card's snippet to the bottom so all three align regardless of how much
     prose sits above them. */
  .recipe pre {
    margin-top: auto;
  }

  .meta {
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0 !important;
    font-size: 0.6rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  .pair {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 320px), 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  /* Quieter than the recipes — supporting detail, not a fourth option. */
  .card--quiet {
    background: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.4);
    box-shadow: none;
    border-style: dashed;
    border-width: 1.5px;
  }

  .detail {
    padding: 1.5rem 1.6rem;
  }

  .detail h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .detail p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
